# {{name}}

A Rusta API project scaffolded with `cargo rusta new --template blog-api`.

## Features

- MongoDB persistence
- JWT authentication with Argon2 password hashing
- APM instrumentation
- Logger integration
- Integration tests with testcontainers
- Docker support

## Quick Start

```bash
# Start MongoDB and the API
docker compose up --build

# Or run locally (requires MongoDB running)
cp .env.example .env
cargo run
```

The API will be available at `http://localhost:3000`.

## Project Structure

```
{{name}}/
├── src/
│   ├── main.rs           # Application entry point
│   ├── lib.rs            # Library exports
│   ├── config.rs         # AppConfig from environment
│   ├── db.rs             # MongoDB initialization
│   ├── errors.rs         # AppError enum
│   ├── middleware/       # JWT guard
│   ├── models/           # Domain types
│   ├── repositories/     # MongoDB-backed repositories
│   ├── services/         # Business logic
│   └── controllers/      # HTTP handlers
├── tests/integration/    # Integration tests with testcontainers
├── Dockerfile
├── docker-compose.yml
└── .env.example
```

## Endpoints

| Method | Path             | Description                              |
| ------ | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| POST   | `/auth/register` | Register a new user (returns JWT + user) |
| POST   | `/auth/login`    | Login (returns JWT + user)               |

## Environment Variables

| Variable             | Description               | Default                     |
| -------------------- | ------------------------- | --------------------------- |
| `SERVER_PORT`        | Server bind address       | `0.0.0.0:3000`              |
| `MONGO_URI`          | MongoDB connection string | `mongodb://localhost:27017` |
| `MONGO_DB`           | Database name             | `{{name}}`                  |
| `JWT_SECRET`         | Secret for signing JWTs   | (required)                  |
| `JWT_EXPIRY_SECONDS` | Token expiry time         | `3600`                      |

## Running Tests

```bash
# Build the test image first
docker build -t {{name}}:test -f {{name}}/Dockerfile .

# Run all tests
cargo test
```
